From 36936f3bf43e33a60e36cff942fa0862e7474645 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NiiRoZz <simonin.remi25@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:24:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] xmem: physical pages, default allocators,
 XMemIsToolsMemAvailable; XMemVirtualAlloc takes 2 MiB pages and placeholders

Serve the seven xmem.dll imports the shim table lacked, with argument shapes
measured at a title's call sites:

- XMemAllocDefault / XMemFreeDefault share XMemAlloc's heap.
- XMemAllocatePhysicalPages / XMemFreePhysicalPages / XMemMapPhysicalPages /
  XMemMapPhysicalPagesScatter: 64 KiB pages of pagefile-backed sections, one
  MapViewOfFile3 view per page in a placeholder window, so pages keep their
  contents across remaps and can alias. Page numbers are non-zero multiples
  of 16 below 2^25; 0 unmaps.
- XMemIsToolsMemAvailable returns FALSE.

XMemVirtualAlloc no longer refuses 2 MiB pages (aligned through
VirtualAlloc2), makes reserve-only 64 KiB regions placeholder windows, and
passes MEM_RESERVE_PLACEHOLDER and MEM_REPLACE_PLACEHOLDER through. The
attribute word and PAGE_GRAPHICS_* handling from #6908 is kept as is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
